    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A union formed in stages in 1948–1950 to merge the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a> into the Indian Union.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana">Maharana of Udaipur</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a> held the top titles, while ministers from popular movements governed.</li><li>It became the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> in January 1950, today <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s largest state by area.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>To soothe local rivalries, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-state-of-greater-rajasthan">Greater Rajasthan</a> put its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a> but its High Court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, which still hosts the principal seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan-high-court">Rajasthan High Court</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

