><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1948</span><span class="rf-text">Nine south-eastern states and two chiefships form a union with its capital at Kota (25 March)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1948</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> joins and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawaharlal-nehru">Nehru</a> inaugurates the United State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> (18 April)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1949</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, Bikaner and Jaisalmer join to form <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-state-of-greater-rajasthan">Greater Rajasthan</a> (30 March)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1949</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsya-union">Matsya Union</a> of Alwar, Bharatpur, Dholpur and Karauli joins (15 May)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1950</span><span class="rf-text">Sirohi joins and the union becomes the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> (26 January)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1956</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-abu">Mount Abu</a> are added and the office of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajpramukh">Rajpramukh</a> abolished</span></li></ol>
